  "id": "generalized-matching-law",
  "term": "generalized matching law",
  "definition": "The generalized matching law is an equation from operant psychology used to describe how behavior reflects the subjective value of available rewards or punishers rather than just their objective properties. It provides a mathematical way to assess sensitivity to features such as frequency, magnitude, or delay when people or animals make choices.",
