      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not directly support the claim that the generalized matching law “is an equation… used to describe how behavior reflects the subjective value of available rewards or punishers rather than just their objective properties.” It mentions perceived (subjective) utility vs physical (objective) value and that some models derived from the generalized matching law quantify scaling, but it does not explicitly define the generalized matching law itself in those terms.",
        "The definition claims the equation applies “when people or animals make choices,” but the packet text provided does not mention animals or establish that scope for the generalized matching law (it only discusses application in operant psychology generally and then the paper’s human IGT context)."
